# Agent Behavior

## Read-Before-Edit Checklist
Before touching any file, confirm you have read the relevant reference:

| File type | Must read first |
|---|---|
| Any component or style file | `docs/design/design-system-contract.md` + `docs/design/pricely-design-system.html` |
| Any page or layout file | `PLAN_FRONTEND.md` |
| Any API route or scraper file | `PLAN_BACKEND.md` |
| Any dependency change | `TECH_STACK.md` |
| Any token or CSS variable | `DESIGN_TOKENS.md` + `src/styles/tokens.css` |

## Execution Model
- Audit first, then implement. Read a file before editing it.
- Remove dead or obsolete code before introducing new files.
- Work in phase order — never skip ahead while an earlier phase has incomplete work:
  1. Foundation (tokens, types, utils)
  2. Shared UI primitives
  3. App shell and navigation
  4. Pages (mock-API-backed)
  5. API route contracts
  6. Data infrastructure (Supabase, Redis)
  7. External provider integrations
  8. Alerts, auth, cron, verdict engine

## Mock → Production Progression
- All API routes start with mock data that exactly matches the `src/types/index.ts` contract.
- Replace mocks with real providers one platform at a time, in order (easiest to hardest).
- Keep mock fallback paths active behind environment variable checks:
  ```typescript
  if (!process.env.SCRAPER_SERVICE_URL) return MOCK_PRICES
  ```
- Local development must never require live credentials to run.

## Editing Policy
- Do not edit files outside the declared scope of the current task.
- Do not leave unused imports, dead variables, commented-out code, or `// TODO` comments in committed files.
- Extend shared modules before creating feature-local duplicates.
- When in doubt whether a component is shared or feature-local, put it in `src/components/` first.

## Verification Policy
- Ask the user for approval before running `npm run lint`, `npx tsc --noEmit`, or `npm run build`.
- Fix all introduced lint and type errors before declaring a phase complete.
- At the end of each phase, summarize: what was **added**, what was **deleted**, what was **changed**, and what **lint/type status** is.

## Files That Are Never Modified
- `docs/design/design-system-contract.md`
- `docs/design/pricely-design-system.html`
- `docs/design/ios-frame.jsx`
- `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `next.config.*`, `.env*`, `.gitignore`
- Any file under `docs/` that is a design reference artifact

## Safety
- Never run destructive git operations (`reset --hard`, `push --force`, `clean -fd`) unless the user explicitly requests it by name.
- Never commit environment variable files.
- Preserve all `.cursor/rules/` files — they are the persistent agent instructions for this project.
